ASoC: soc-core: start the rtd component list empty

devm_kzalloc_flex() sets the __counted_by counter (rtd->num_components) to the
allocated size, but snd_soc_rtd_add_component() appends at num_components. On
7.4-rc2 every component therefore lands past slots that stay NULL, and
for_each_rtd_components() stops at the first NULL: soc_probe_link_components()
probes nothing, no component DAPM widgets exist, all routes fail and the card
never registers (Galaxy Book4 Edge: no audio, wcd938x set_jack -22).

--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -387,6 +387,9 @@
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
+	/* kzalloc_flex set the counter to the size; snd_soc_rtd_add_component() counts from 0 */
+	rtd->num_components = 0;
+
 	rtd->dev = dev;
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&rtd->list);
 	for_each_pcm_streams(stream) {
